# First Bark: the smallest Dynamic Dialog scene. One character (Pip), this one rule file.
#
# Pip's Dialog Speaker has Idle Talk switched on, so every few seconds it asks the rules
# "what does Pip say for the TalkIdle concept?". Every rule whose conditions all pass is a
# candidate, and the one with the most conditions wins.
#
# Save this file while the scene is playing and Pip uses your edits straight away.

# Wins first: it is the only rule that checks a fact Pip doesn't have yet.
rule Hello
  concept TalkIdle
  if barks missing
  say "Oh! Hello there. I'm Pip."
  remember barks = 1

# The fallback: no conditions besides the concept, so anything more specific beats it.
# With several lines, one is picked at random each time.
rule Chatter
  concept TalkIdle
  say "Nice weather for standing around."
  say "Did you know I'm made of one rule file?"
  say "Try editing FirstBark.dlg while I talk."
  say "Every line I say is counted in my memory."
  remember barks += 1

# Pip remembers how often they have talked (the "barks" fact) and gets tired after a while.
rule Tired
  concept TalkIdle
  if barks >= 5
  say "That's everything I know. Write me some more rules!"
  remember barks = 1
